{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.QLieBracket","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.QLieBracket","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.SubstrateParameter"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qLieBracket_classical","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qLieBracket_classical","kind":"theorem","line":35,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-lie-bracket.lean#L35-L39","doc":"The q-deformed Lie bracket recovers the classical bracket at `q = 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.qLieBracket","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.qLieBracket","kind":"def","line":21,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-lie-bracket.lean#L21-L33","doc":"**q-Deformed Lie bracket**:\n`[V, W]_q = q⁻¹ [V, W] + (1 − q⁻¹)(θ(V) ℒ_ξ W − θ(W) ℒ_ξ V)`.\n\nHere `bracket_VW = [V, W]` is the classical bracket value,\n`thetaV_LxiW = θ(V) ℒ_ξ W` and `thetaW_LxiV = θ(W) ℒ_ξ V`, all\nevaluated pointwise at `p : M`, with `q = sp.field p`.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{def:q-lie-bracket}` ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:ex:q-lie-bracket","label":"ex:q-lie-bracket","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/q-lie-bracket.md"}],"signatureChunk":0}]}